 :question/id #uuid "5924d1cc-a3c0-5262-9e69-f815649c0188" :question/math-academy-id "q-51140" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-23x+27}{x(x-3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-3}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x-3)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-23x+27=A(x-3)^{2}+Bx(x-3)+Cx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(3)^{2}-23(3)+27 & =A(3-3)^{2}+B\\cdot 3(3-3)+C\\cdot 3 \\\\ 36-69+27 & =3C \\\\ -6 & =3C \\\\ C & =\\frac{(-6)}{3} \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-23(0)+27 & =A(0-3)^{2}+B(0)(0-3)+C(0) \\\\ 27 & =9A \\\\ A & =\\frac{27}{9} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1)^{2}-23(1)+27 & =3(1-3)^{2}+B(1)(1-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\ 4-23+27 & =12-2B-2 \\\\ 8 & =10-2B \\\\ 2B & =2 \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2)=-6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51140/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51140"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346933/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "25585920-0307-5d6e-9991-69cc1ee57b23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346933/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a58e3c1a-b91b-5a4e-aec4-9681b3887f80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346933/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-346933/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c