^{2}-5x+9=A(x+2)^{2}+B(x+2)+C.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}-5(-2)+9 & =A(-2+2)^{2}+B(-2+2)+C \\\\ 27 & =A(0)^{2}+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}-5(-1)+9 & =A(-1+2)^{2}+B(-1+2)+27 \\\\ 16 & =A+B+27 \\\\ B & =-A-11.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)^{2}-5(0)+9 & =A(0+2)^{2}+B(0+2)+27 \\\\ 9 & =4A+2B+27 \\\\ 2B & =-4A-18 \\\\ B & =-2A-9.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-A-11 & =-2A-9 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-2-11 \\\\ B & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{2}{x+2}-\\frac{13}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{27}{(x+2)^{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346933/field-1" "q-346933/field-2" "q-346933/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346933"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70014/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "7b9ade5c-8e7b-5c12-8580-428fdeb62b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70014/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "25f25cbe-1a62-5953-b2f6-b3c73a9a69c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70014/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "45f51ef0-be7a-5034-a80b-5ec0052988be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70014/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "7c553d61-0497-5f72-92f0-3d5f1ccd7e85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70014/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "e9da05ca-c076-5e95-8777-394303993b78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70014/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7c5f86-014b-59b3-8e24-b22ab1027219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70014/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-70014/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-70014/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-70014/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-70014/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-70014/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70014" :question/id #uuid "ba70f430-e2d4-5628-aab6-590cad6bcdca" :question/math-academy-id "q-70014" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-{x}^{2}-3x-1}{x(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB-CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x+1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-3x-1=A(x+1)^{3}+Bx(x+1)^{2}+Cx(x+1)+Dx.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(-1)^{2}-3(-1)-1 & =A(-1+1)^{3}+B(-1)(-1+1)^{2}+C(-1)(-1+1)+D(-1) \\\\ -1+3-1 & =-D \\\\ 1 & =-D \\\\ D & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(0)^{2}-3(0)-1 & =A(0+1)^{3}+B(0)(0+1)^{2}+C(0)(0+1)+D(0) \\\\ -1 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(1)^{2}-3(1)-1 & =(-1)(1+1)^{3}+B(1)(1+1)^{2}+C(1)(1+1)+(-1)(1) \\\\ -1-3-1 & =-8+4B+2C-1 \\\\ 2C & =4-4B \\\\ C & =2-2B.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(2)^{2}-3(2)-1 & =(-1)(2+1)^{3}+B(2)(2+1)^{2}+C(2)(2+1)+(-1)(2) \\\\ -4-6-1 & =-27+18B+6C-2 \\\\ 6C & =18-18B \\\\ C & =3-3B.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-2B & =3-3B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $C:$\n\n$$\nC=2-2(1)=0\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=(-1)(1)-0(-1)=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-70014/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70014"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115217/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "39829550-7004-53e5-b564-8623835dcc2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115217/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "7490c296-a429-5bbe-8a88-4de6d208544e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115217/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "0a813a2f-8211-5b0f-b302-0e10563a927f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115217/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "bef828b4-f4f6-5fb3-97aa-4f3a3ca173f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115217/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "f3f0438a-26a0-5658-9b73-e1e403b3bfca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115217/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a54fe70-041d-574e-ac56-5577dfc202bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115217/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer-field/choices ["q-115217/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-115217/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-115217/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-115217/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-115217/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115217" :question/id #uuid "4a5215de-daa3-58f1-a6d7-6048ff9631f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-115217" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-7x+8}{(x-1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-7x+8 & =A(x-1)^{2}+B(x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}-7(1)+8 & =A(1-1)^{2}+B(1-1)+C \\\\ 4 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}-7(0)+8 & =A(0-1)^{2}+B(0-1)+4 \\\\ 8 & =A-B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A-B-4 \\\\ B & =A-4.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2)^{2}-7(2)+8 & =A(2-1)^{2}+B(2-1)+4 \\\\ 6 & =A+B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A+B-2 \\\\ B & =2-A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4 & =2-A \\\\ 2A & =6 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-4=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 4=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115217/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351243/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "d3dbfefe-5ba0-542d-93a2-d810fd9a194e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186266401 :answer-field/choices ["q-351243/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69993/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "1aa237f8-ec8e-5d3c-98e6-47c4ef2fb251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69993/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "89ed8dae-5af5-5e25-a60c-1c791a37071d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69993/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "73fa4984-4874-512c-98b9-7b553a96ad20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69993/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "b79de1f8-8ac2-55b5-a65d-f66b1688db28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69993/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9090becb-9b60-5689-93aa-e1cce55078c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69993/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4926f5c2-9d7a-58ab-a2db-0f7e7f08eb4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69993/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-69993/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-69993/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-69993/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-69993/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-69993/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69993" :question/id #uuid "7d3ec213-68d1-51ee-bba2-3f8b41242807" :question/math-academy-id "q-69993" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+3x}{(x-1)(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, find the value of $AB-CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)(x+1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n1+3x=A(x+1)^{3}+B(x-1)(x+1)^{2}+C(x-1)(x+1)+D(x-1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(-1) & =A(-1+1)^{3}+B(-1-1)(-1+1)^{2}+C(-1-1)(-1+1)+D(-1-1) \\\\ 1-3 & =-2D \\\\ -2 & =-2D \\\\ D & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(1) & =A(1+1)^{3}+B(1-1)(1+1)^{2}+C(1-1)(1+1)+D(1-1) \\\\ 1+3 & =8A \\\\ 4 & =8A \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+1)^{3}+B(0-1)(0+1)^{2}+C(0-1)(0+1)+1(0-1) \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}-B-C-1 \\\\ C & =-\\frac{3}{2}-B.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+1)^{3}+B(2-1)(2+1)^{2}+C(2-1)(2+1)+1(2-1) \\\\ 1+6 & =\\frac{27}{2}+9B+3C+1 \\\\ 3C & =-\\frac{15}{2}-9B \\\\ C & =-\\frac{5}{2}-3B.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}-B & =-\\frac{5}{2}-3B \\\\ 2B & =-1 \\\\ B & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $C:$\n\n$$\nC=-\\frac{3}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})-(-1)(1)=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-69993/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69993"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12333"] :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7x+6}{(x+2)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} -\\dfrac{8}{(x+2)^2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+6 & =A(x+2)-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A.$\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-2,$ since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x.$ So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0.$\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+6 & =A(x+2)-8 \\\\ 7(0)+6 & =A(0+2)-8 \\\\ 6 & =2A-8 \\\\ 14 & =2A \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12334"] :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7-4x}{(x+5)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+5} +\\dfrac{B}{(x+5)^2},\n$$\n\nfind the values of $A$ and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to solve for $A$ and $B,$ and both of these constants appear in the equation simultaneously. However, we can eliminate $A$ if we substitute $x=-5.$\n\nPlugging $x=-5$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+B \\\\ 7-4(-5) & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ 27 & =A(0)+B \\\\ 27 & =0+B \\\\ 27 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve for $A.$ To do this, let’s start by substituting our value $B=27$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A.$\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-5,$ since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x.$ So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0.$\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+27 \\\\ 7-4(0) & =A(0+5)+27 \\\\ 7 & =5A+27 \\\\ -20 & =5A \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=-4$ and $B=27.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12335"] :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{C}{(x+1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the expression through by $(x-3)^2(x+1)$ to give\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-3)^2.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3$ eliminates the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(3)^{2}-5(3)+8=B\\cdot 4\\,⟹\\,B=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)^{2}-5(-1)+8=C\\cdot (-4)^{2}\\,⟹\\,C=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUnfortunately, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to eliminate both $B$ and $C.$ However, using our results for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+5(x+1)+1(x-3)^2,\n$$\n\nand we can plug in any value of $x$ to solve for $A.$ Let's choose the simplest number to plug in, $x=0.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =A(0-3)(0+1)+5(0+1)+C(0-3)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =-3A+5+9 \\\\ -6 & =-3A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=2\\cdot 5\\cdot 1=10,\n$$\n\nand the partial fraction decomposition is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{2}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{5}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12336"] :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1-2x}{(x+1)(x+2)^3}= \\dfrac{A}{x+1}+\\dfrac{B}{x+2} +\\dfrac{C}{(x+2)^2} + \\dfrac{D}{(x+2)^3},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB + CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)(x+2)^3$ gives\n\n$$\n1 - 2x = A(x+2)^3 + B(x+1)(x+2)^2 + C(x+1)(x+2) + D(x+1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(-2) & =A(-2+2)^{3}+B(-2+1)(-2+2)^{2}+C(-2+1)(-2+2)+D(-2+1) \\\\ 1+4 & =-D \\\\ D & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(-1) & =A(-1+2)^{3}+B(-1+1)(-1+2)^{2}+C(-1+1)(-1+2)+D(-1+1) \\\\ 1+2 & =A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = 0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(0) & =3(0+2)^{3}+B(0+1)(0+2)^{2}+C(0+1)(0+2)+(-5)(0+1) \\\\ 1-0 & =24+4B+2C-5 \\\\ 2C & =-4B-18 \\\\ C & =-2B-9.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x = 1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(1) & =A(1+2)^{3}+B(1+1)(1+2)^{2}+C(1+1)(1+2)+D(1+1) \\\\ 1-2 & =81+18B+6C-10 \\\\ 6C & =-18B-72 \\\\ C & =-3B-12.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2B-9 & =-3B-12 \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $C{:}$\n\n$$\nC = -2(-3) - 9 = -3\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB + CD = 3(-3) + (-3)(-5) = 6.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
